1841	      screen pixels we're using, and convert to RGB.
1842	
1843	      We add some 'bloom', variations in the horizontal scan width with
1844	      the amount of brightness, extremely common on period TV sets. They
1845	      had a single oscillator which generated both the horizontal scan and
1846	      (during the horizontal retrace interval) the high voltage for the
1847	      electron beam. More brightness meant more load on the oscillator,
1848	      which caused an decrease in horizontal deflection. Look for
1849	      (bloomthisrow).
